@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@ No `patches.py`; `dm/tools/sdk_patches.py`'s SDK-wide rules cut its `sdk` build
 
 - RomFS is almost entirely Yaz0-compressed SARC (`*.szs`).
 - 7,258 shaders: bfsha (BNSH) in `ShaderData`, agl sharcb (BAHS) and layout BNSH in `SystemData`, particle effects in `EffectData` and 40 BNSH in `main`, all with Mario's binding layout (every binding decodes). The one that does not build is the fin fur geometry shader (`RenderFinFur`), as in 3D World: Metal has no geometry stage.
+- **Resolved: duplicate representative labels (2026-11-21, [issue #2924](https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/issues/2924)).** Checked first-copy selection (`8d62601f`) over the registered v393216 `main` (`41eae379…`, 96 embedded BNSH occurrences reducing to 40 keys with byte-identical duplicate control sections and code) updates 36 rows in [`shader_map.tsv`](shader_map.tsv) (22 source labels and 14 package indices). All 7,258 shader keys, stages, packages, non-`main` rows, `shader_facts.tsv`, `shader_pairs.tsv`, and `pso_pairs.tsv` remain unchanged. Shared mechanism: [The split shader tables differ from a game profile's](../../../docs/reference/packing.md#the-split-shader-tables-differ-from-a-game-profiles).
 - `main` imports `glslcCompile` and holds agl's GLSL sources, but no module defines it, so nothing is compiled at run time. `shader_split.py` now asks for captured GLSLC outputs only when a module of the profile defines `glslcCompile`, as `profile_guess.py` does.
 - Shared fonts: it records them as plain TTFs and calls `Decode` only for its BFTTF formats (SDK 8: the address is the TTF).
 
